# ============================================================================
# CORRECTION APPLIED 2026-07-27 (team-lead requirement verification)
# ============================================================================
# The initial finding was factually incorrect. The recommendation to reject
# localhost/127.0.0.1 at the CLI command layer contradicts the explicit
# acceptance criterion in sprint-ai-22 (line 143-144).
#
# WHAT WAS WRONG:
# - Original claim: "InterfaceCommand::run_with_store() and TrustCommand::
#   run_with_store() pass --bind, --advertise-host, and --host flags through
#   unrestricted HostName parsing with no loopback/localhost rejection at the
#   command layer." — this is treated as a defect requiring command-layer
#   rejection.
# - ROOT CAUSE: Misreading of REQ-CORE-TRANSPORT-002C and AI.22 requirements.
#   The finding assumed loopback must be rejected at the command boundary.
#
# CORRECTED REQUIREMENT (sprint-ai-22, lines 143-144):
# "`localhost` and `127.0.0.1` are parsing/host-preservation regressions only;
# they may not be used to satisfy the virtual-Ethernet same-host proof."
#
# INTERPRETATION:
# - "parsing/host-preservation regressions" = must parse successfully
# - CLI commands (--bind, --advertise-host, --host) MUST accept valid
#   loopback literals per AI.22 acceptance criteria
# - Required test coverage: self-send exemption tests with localhost
#   destinations, host-preservation regression tests per AI.22 (see
#   sprint doc at line 20-22)
# - "may not be used to satisfy" = downstream enforcement concern
#   (evidence validation does not accept loopback-sourced proof for real
#   same-host proof), not a command-layer rejection concern
# - Parsing loopback at the CLI is REQUIRED behavior, not a defect
#
# ACTUAL STATUS:
# - CLI peer commands correctly accept syntactically valid loopback
#   literals per AI.22 acceptance criteria
# - The original "command-layer rejection" recommendation is INVALID and
#   superseded
# - No CLI-layer code change needed for loopback rejection
# - Downstream evidence-validation enforcement (that loopback cannot satisfy
#   the real same-host proof) is already in scope for AI.22 QA
#
# CONCLUSION:
# - This finding was purely misdirected; no command-layer defect exists
# - Closing finding as WAIVED per AI.22 requirement clarification
# ============================================================================

<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI30-VALIDATION-001>
  triage:status "closed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:correctionNote "Finding superseded by sprint-ai-22 acceptance criterion (line 143-144): 'localhost' and '127.0.0.1' are parsing/host-preservation regressions only; they may not be used to satisfy the virtual-Ethernet same-host proof. CLI commands (--bind, --advertise-host, --host) MUST accept loopback literals for test coverage per AI.22. The original recommendation to reject at command layer contradicts the explicit requirement that parsing must succeed. Downstream enforcement (ensuring loopback-sourced evidence cannot satisfy real proof) is covered by AI.22 QA scope." ;
  triage:waiverReason "Misdirected finding based on misreading of AI.22 requirement. CLI acceptance of loopback is required behavior." ;
  triage:correctionAppliedAt "2026-07-27T15:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:correctionAppliedBy "team-lead (requirement verification)" ;
  triage:referencedSprintRequirement "sprint-ai-22-loopback-self-send-exemption.md lines 143-144" .
